  "description": "42 GREAT EASTERN ST",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed advertisement hoarding, by reason of its location, scale and detailed design, would have an unacceptable impact upon public safety and highway visibility to the detriment of vehicular and pedestrian safety. As such, the proposal would be contrary to policies D8 (Public Realm), T1 (Strategic Approach to Transport), T2 (Healthy Streets), T4 (Assessing and Mitigating Transport Impacts) of the London Plan (2021) and policies PP1 (Public Realm), LP41 (Liveable Neighbourhoods), LP42 (Walking and Cycling), LP43 (Transport and Development) of Hackney&#x27;s Local Development Plan (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed advertisement hoarding by reason of its size, detailed design, position and location, would result in an obtrusive form of development which would adversely affect the visual amenity, character, significance and appearance of the host Grade II Listed Building, the South Shoreditch Conservation Area, and the surrounding area. As such, the proposal would be contrary to Policy D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design-led Approach), D8 (Public Realm) and HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), LP7 (Advertisements) and PP1 (Public Realm) of Hackney&#x27;s Local Development Plan (2020).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
